	(text "Task 13 audit fix (F3, minor): D29/R120 -- spec S10 12V-node/power indicator, missing since Task 4 dropped the LED (drift, never amended). LED_PWR->R120(1k)->D29->GND. LED_PWR is only alive when +3V3 is up, which -- per the F1 fix pass (R40/R41 BUCK_EN divider corrected) -- only happens once the +12V node has been negotiated (buck now reliably starts ~8V+, never at 5V pre-negotiation). So D29 correctly indicates negotiated-12V-present, not raw VBUS. It is killable via the LED_PWR switch/GPIO like the other LED_PWR-domain indicators (RGB, WWAN)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 555 160 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "84423a43-f8be-4b72-aca3-f902777a8f06")
	)
	(text "Task 13 audit fix (F3, minor): D30/R121 -- spec S10 PD-good indicator, missing since Task 4 dropped the LED. LED_PWR->R121(1k)->D30->CH224K_PG. CH224K_PG is open-drain, active-low (WCH CH224K datasheet: pulls to GND once PD negotiation succeeds; datasheet explicitly lists driving an indicator LED as a typical use). Checked R4 (10k pull-up, CH224K_PG to +3V3, from Task 4): it does NOT conflict with D30 -- it defines a clean idle-high (LED off) state when PG is unasserted and adds only ~0.33mA of extra sink current when PG pulls low (LED on); R4 is kept as-is, not replaced."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 168 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "2dbbc2c9-b07b-4394-bc61-9338411c0407")
	)
